ir3: fit every wave of a barrier workgroup in the register file

A barrier keeps all the waves of a workgroup resident at once, so they share
the register file rather than getting it in turn, and nothing on a5xx bounds
them against it.  A GLES 3.1 compute shader with a barrier faults the GPU as
soon as its waves want more than the file holds.

calc_limit_pressure_for_cs_with_barrier() computes that bound but applies it
only with merged registers, where one limit covers the whole file.  Its TODO
asks for the split-bank case to be done after the first pressure pass, because
how the budget divides between the two banks depends on how much half the
shader uses.  Return the bound rather than applying it, so that case can clamp
the file both banks are sized against once that is known.  A variable
workgroup size is bounded from the largest the API allows, as it already was
with merged registers.

The wave-pair count was taken at the threadsize the shader runs, which cancels
against the divisor below: a double-sized wave halves the count and then costs
two parts per vec4 instead of one.  Where the banks are split, count
single-sized pairs so that only the divisor carries the threadsize.  Sweeping
workgroup size against register footprint on a db820c, 128 threads of 17
registers fault where the old formula permits 32, and 16 run.

A wave's share can now be smaller than the half bank, so the half budget is
clamped to it as well; without that the full budget underflows into a bound
that allows everything.

